						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Guys,<br />
<br />
Aamain can kill me if he wishes later - but I don't believe it is the intent to hide this information.  I also dont believe in with holding information because &quot;knowledge is power&quot;.<br />
<br />
The officers have a dedicated chat channel.  All officers contact myself or aamain in-game to find out the password.<br />
<br />
To log in type:<br />
<br />
/join oono:password<br />
<br />
to use type /list to see which channel you have it on (1-10) then type:<br />
<br />
/1 message (if it is channel 1)<br />
<br />
To log in automatically (affects everyone of your chars) type:<br />
<br />
/autojoin oono:password, tradeskills <br />
<br />
(ok only use the second if you want to be on that channel also hehe)<br />
<br />
The purpose of this channel is so that we can stay in communication at all times and so that we don't air all of our laundry in guildchat.<br />
<br />
Any member that wants to speak to more then one officer can ask to be added to the channel.  The moderator types:<br />
<br />
/chat invite [channel]  channel = 1-10<br />
<br />
This is a one time only invite that gets around the password.  If you are invited type:<br />
<br />
/join &lt;channelname&gt;    channel name = oono<br />
<br />
Please take any problems that should not be aired in guild chat to this channel.<br />
<br />
To see everyone on a specific channel type:<br />
/list 1<br />
<br />
If you need to speak to a select few officers make your own channel and invite who you need with tells.<br />
<br />
/join mych  (you become the moderator)<br />
<br />
You can also use this if people are hunting together in a zone - but are in more then one group.<br />
<br />
Have fun, drink, and passout :0						</td>
